cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ALE-MTL in your research, please cite the software and the accompanying SoftwareX article when available."
type: software
title: "ALE-MTL: Accumulated Local Effects for Multi-task Learning"
version: "0.1.0"
license: "BSD-3-Clause"
authors:
  - name: "ALE-MTL contributors"
abstract: >-
  ALE-MTL is a Python/PyTorch toolkit for building, training, explaining, and
  comparing multi-task learning models. The software computes task-wise
  Accumulated Local Effects profiles and estimates task relationships using
  curve similarity, including Frechet-based similarity scores.
keywords:
  - "accumulated local effects"
  - "explainable artificial intelligence"
  - "Frechet distance"
  - "multi-task learning"
  - "PyTorch"
  - "task similarity"
repository-code: "https://github.com/papabloblo/alemtl"

